#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:104
msgid "How It Works"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:106
msgid "Startup Discovery"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:108
msgid ""
"When Hermes Agent starts, `discover_mcp_tools()` is called during tool "
"initialization:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:110
msgid "Reads `mcp_servers` from `~/.hermes/config.yaml`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:111
msgid "For each server, spawns a connection in a dedicated background event loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:112
msgid ""
"Initializes the MCP session and calls `list_tools()` to discover "
"available tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:113
msgid "Registers each tool in the Hermes tool registry"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:115
msgid "Tool Naming Convention"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:117
msgid "MCP tools are registered with the naming pattern:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:123
msgid ""
"Hyphens and dots in names are replaced with underscores for LLM API "
"compatibility."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:125
msgid "Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:126
msgid "Server `filesystem`, tool `read_file` → `mcp_filesystem_read_file`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:127
msgid "Server `github`, tool `list-issues` → `mcp_github_list_issues`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:128
msgid "Server `my-api`, tool `fetch.data` → `mcp_my_api_fetch_data`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:130
msgid "Auto-Injection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:132
msgid ""
"After discovery, MCP tools are automatically injected into all `hermes-*`"
" platform toolsets (CLI, Discord, Telegram, etc.). This means MCP tools "
"are available in every conversation without any additional configuration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:134
msgid "Connection Lifecycle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:136
msgid ""
"Each server runs as a long-lived asyncio Task in a background daemon "
"thread"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:137
msgid "Connections persist for the lifetime of the agent process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:138
msgid ""
"If a connection drops, automatic reconnection with exponential backoff "
"kicks in (up to 5 retries, max 60s backoff)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:139
msgid "On agent shutdown, all connections are gracefully closed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:141
msgid "Idempotency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:143
msgid ""
"`discover_mcp_tools()` is idempotent -- calling it multiple times only "
"connects to servers that aren't already connected. Failed servers are "
"retried on subsequent calls."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:145
msgid "Transport Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:147
msgid "Stdio Transport"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:149
msgid ""
"The most common transport. Hermes launches the MCP server as a subprocess"
" and communicates over stdin/stdout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:158
msgid ""
"The subprocess inherits a **filtered** environment (see Security section "
"below) plus any variables you specify in `env`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:160
msgid "HTTP / StreamableHTTP Transport"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:162
msgid ""
"For remote or shared MCP servers. Requires the `mcp` package to include "
"HTTP client support (`mcp.client.streamable_http`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:172
msgid ""
"If HTTP support is not available in your installed `mcp` version, the "
"server will fail with an ImportError and other servers will continue "
"normally."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:174
msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:176
msgid "Environment Variable Filtering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:178
msgid ""
"For stdio servers, Hermes does NOT pass your full shell environment to "
"MCP subprocesses. Only safe baseline variables are inherited:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:180
msgid "`PATH`, `HOME`, `USER`, `LANG`, `LC_ALL`, `TERM`, `SHELL`, `TMPDIR`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:181
msgid "Any `XDG_*` variables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:183
msgid ""
"All other environment variables (API keys, tokens, secrets) are excluded "
"unless you explicitly add them via the `env` config key. This prevents "
"accidental credential leakage to untrusted MCP servers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:195
msgid "Credential Stripping in Error Messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:197
msgid ""
"If an MCP tool call fails, any credential-like patterns in the error "
"message are automatically redacted before being shown to the LLM. This "
"covers:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:199
msgid "GitHub PATs (`ghp_...`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:200
msgid "OpenAI-style keys (`sk-...`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:201
msgid "Bearer tokens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:202
msgid "Generic `token=`, `key=`, `API_KEY=`, `password=`, `secret=` patterns"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:204
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:206
msgid "\"MCP SDK not available -- skipping MCP tool discovery\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:208
msgid "The `mcp` Python package is not installed. Install it:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:214
msgid "\"No MCP servers configured\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:216
msgid ""
"No `mcp_servers` key in `~/.hermes/config.yaml`, or it's empty. Add at "
"least one server."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:218
msgid "\"Failed to connect to MCP server 'X'\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:220
msgid "Common causes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:221
msgid ""
"**Command not found**: The `command` binary isn't on PATH. Ensure `npx`, "
"`uvx`, or the relevant command is installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:222
msgid ""
"**Package not found**: For npx servers, the npm package may not exist or "
"may need `-y` in args to auto-install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:223
msgid ""
"**Timeout**: The server took too long to start. Increase "
"`connect_timeout`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:224
msgid "**Port conflict**: For HTTP servers, the URL may be unreachable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:226
msgid ""
"\"MCP server 'X' requires HTTP transport but mcp.client.streamable_http "
"is not available\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:228
msgid "Your `mcp` package version doesn't include HTTP client support. Upgrade:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:234
msgid "Tools not appearing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:236
msgid ""
"Check that the server is listed under `mcp_servers` (not `mcp` or "
"`servers`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:237
msgid "Ensure the YAML indentation is correct"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:238
msgid "Look at Hermes Agent startup logs for connection messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:239
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Tool names are prefixed with `mcp_{server}_{tool}` -- look for that "
"pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:241
msgid "Connection keeps dropping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:243
msgid ""
"The client retries up to 5 times with exponential backoff (1s, 2s, 4s, "
"8s, 16s, capped at 60s). If the server is fundamentally unreachable, it "
"gives up after 5 attempts. Check the server process and network "
"connectivity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:245
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:247
msgid "Time Server (uvx)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:256
msgid "Registers tools like `mcp_time_get_current_time`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:258
msgid "Filesystem Server (npx)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:268
msgid ""
"Registers tools like `mcp_filesystem_read_file`, "
"`mcp_filesystem_write_file`, `mcp_filesystem_list_directory`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:270
msgid "GitHub Server with Authentication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:282
msgid ""
"Registers tools like `mcp_github_list_issues`, "
"`mcp_github_create_pull_request`, etc."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:284
msgid "Remote HTTP Server"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:297
msgid "Multiple Servers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:322
msgid ""
"All tools from all servers are registered and available simultaneously. "
"Each server's tools are prefixed with its name to avoid collisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:324
msgid "Sampling (Server-Initiated LLM Requests)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:326
msgid ""
"Hermes supports MCP's `sampling/createMessage` capability — MCP servers "
"can request LLM completions through the agent during tool execution. This"
" enables agent-in-the-loop workflows (data analysis, content generation, "
"decision-making)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:328
msgid "Sampling is **enabled by default**. Configure per server:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:346
msgid ""
"Servers can also include `tools` in sampling requests for multi-turn "
"tool-augmented workflows. The `max_tool_rounds` config prevents infinite "
"tool loops. Per-server audit metrics (requests, errors, tokens, tool use "
"count) are tracked via `get_mcp_status()`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:348
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Disable sampling for untrusted servers with `sampling: { enabled: false "
"}`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:350
msgid "Notes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:352
msgid ""
"MCP tools are called synchronously from the agent's perspective but run "
"asynchronously on a dedicated background event loop"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:353
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Tool results are returned as JSON with either `{\"result\": \"...\"}` or "
"`{\"error\": \"...\"}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:354
msgid ""
"The native MCP client is independent of `mcporter` -- you can use both "
"simultaneously"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:355
msgid ""
"Server connections are persistent and shared across all conversations in "
"the same agent process"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/native-mcp_SKILL.md:356
msgid ""
"Adding or removing servers requires restarting the agent (no hot-reload "
"currently)"
msgstr ""

